{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788163036,"nonce":"BAkt4yU5MJnhVWG11i7NHU1mfIc=","message":"Fixed in bd6eaea on `docs/ci-simplification`. `image.yml`'s build matrix is now\nselected per image by a `changes` job reading the same `.github/path-filters.yml`\nthat `ci.yml` uses (6729fc2), so a stylesheet rebuilds `scarab-server` — the\nonly image with an npm stage — and nothing else.\n\nTwo things worth recording:\n\n1. The workflow-level `pull_request: paths:` filter was REMOVED, not kept. It\n   was the second filtering mechanism this ticket warned about: an outer union\n   that has to track four inner filters, and it was ALREADY out of step — it\n   never listed `rust-toolchain.toml`, which both cargo-built images read. A\n   docs-only PR now runs one ~15s `changes` job that selects `[]`.\n2. The context/dockerfile mapping could not stay in `include:`. With a dynamic\n   `image` list, an `include` entry whose `image` is not in the matrix does not\n   filter itself out — GitHub appends it as a NEW combination with no\n   `platform` and no `runner`. It is a `case` step now, with an explicit\n   `::error::` on an unmapped image so a fifth image cannot be added to one\n   place and not the other.\n\nAll four images still build on push to main and on `v*` tags: a `sha-\u003csha\u003e` tag\nthat exists for some images and not others is a trap you only discover in a\ndeploy (`kind.yml`, `just local-helm sha-\u003csha\u003e`, the chart). Selection is a\nPR-only economy.","files":null}]}